{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 12 that avoid forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". Classic count of binary strings with no run of 3 same bits. Equivalent to sequences with no 3 consecutive 0s or 1s. Count via recurrence. Let a_n be number of length n strings ending with run of length 1 of some bit? We can use DP with states: last two bits? Actually need to avoid 3 same. So track last two bits and last bit? Simpler: Let f(n, k, b) where k is length of current run (1 or 2) and b is bit value. Recurrence: from state (k,b) we can add same bit if k<2, else must switch. Count.\n\nInitialize for n=1: two states: run length1 bit0, run length1 bit1. So f(1,1,0)=1, f(1,1,1)=1.\n\nFor n>1: f(n,1,b) = sum over previous states where we switched bit: f(n-1,1,1-b)+f(n-1,2,1-b). f(n,2,b) = f(n-1,1,b) (since only from run length1 same bit). Cannot have run length>2.\n\nCompute up to n=12.\n\nLet's compute iteratively.\n\nI'll create table for n, counts for (1,0),(2,0),(1,1),(2,1).\n\nn=1:\n(1,0)=1\n(2,0)=0\n(1,1)=1\n(2,1)=0\n\nn=2:\nCompute (1,0)= f(1,1,1)+f(1,2,1)=1+0=1\n(2,0)= f(1,1,0)=1\n(1,1)= f(1,1,0)+f(1,2,0)=1+0=1\n(2,1)= f(1,1,1)=1\n\nn=3:\n(1,0)= f(2,1,1)+f(2,2,1)=1+1=2\n(2,0)= f(2,1,0)=1\n(1,1)= f(2,1,0)+f(2,2,0)=1+1=2\n(2,1)= f(2,1,1)=1\n\nn=4:\n(1,0)= f(3,1,1)+f(3,2,1)=2+1=3\n(2,0)= f(3,1,0)=2\n(1,1)= f(3,1,0)+f(3,2,0)=2+1=3\n(2,1)= f(3,1,1)=2\n\nn=5:\n(1,0)= f(4,1,1)+f(4,2,1)=3+2=5\n(2,0)= f(4,1,0)=3\n(1,1)= f(4,1,0)+f(4,2,0)=3+2=5\n(2,1)= f(4,1,1)=3\n\nn=6:\n(1,0)= f(5,1,1)+f(5,2,1)=5+3=8\n(2,0)= f(5,1,0)=5\n(1,1)= f(5,1,0)+f(5,2,0)=5+3="}}],"created":1790938523,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4111,"total_tokens":4879,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_t